Problem Statement:
Generation of camera extrinsics of a virtual camera for a given 3D face model using any partial view image of the 3D face model taken from the virtual camera and its intrinsics. 
Given a 3D Face model and partial view images of the 3D model captured by the virtual cameras from any view, the camera extrinsics matrix should be obtained.
The 3D face mesh and the partial view images may contain a neutral expression or a deformed expression. 
With the obtained accurate camera extrinsics, different partial view images should be generated for the same virtual camera. 

Pipeline for Camera Extrinsic Prediction and Application:
Module 1: Given a face mesh, and a partial view image of the face mesh, develop an ML model to estimate the camera extrinsics of the virtual cameras for the corresponding partial view image.
Module 2: Having a robust pipeline for Module 1, generate different partial view images using Pytorch3D for the same face mesh using camera extrinsics obtained from Module 1.

Verification Metrics:
Perceptual loss.
Landmark consistency loss (2D-3D)
Per-pixel loss.

